  "code": "2817",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong>Note</strong></p>\n<p>1. Auto Immune reactivity are not by themselves diagnostic and must be correlated with other laboratory<br>2. and clinical findings.<br>3. Test conducted on undiluted CSF.<br>4. Antigen substrate - transfected cells of EU-90.<br>5. ~ 14% anti NMDAR encephalitis patients have antibodies only in CSF.</p>\n<p><strong>Comments</strong></p>\n<p>Auto antibodies against glutamate receptors (NMDA type) are specific markers for anti glutamate receptor type encephalitis.<br>This is an inflammatory encephalopathic autoimmune disease and still widely under diagnosed. This is frequently associated&nbsp;with ovarian and testicular teratoma</p>",
